[{:db/id "q-8099/selection/14dda16bf3677b40c9d18d46b6a541ed3bdbc1f25448258db1986eb44d9d45aa" :answer/id #uuid "d95ef9b8-e044-562a-b6d9-164991953aba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{4x}-2x{e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8099/selection/00460e20ed1d34c197a9be20e011dd597acdbfb2a07560e00454b71d68378cf5" :answer/id #uuid "ff7abd06-2b44-5056-9ab8-de0a3c016dba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{4x}-2{e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8099/selection/88feea0645bd98b57357f3aaa8e168684e33a9f5b1ef4970d8a733361ae568be" :answer/id #uuid "55d818ac-b75b-5bbc-a975-8fbd0b864e65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{2x}+{e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8099/selection/c3a41f59c04230b11372818321cc594550e1fc29de294c5d1c4649034da36d32" :answer/id #uuid "0ce8b116-01ef-5dd4-b47e-7ca5f852fdc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{4x}+x{e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8099/selection/393fe52ac9ccbb50900a0186b5548c3ae356a1b24ddf8f51fb4d31101b3d16ec" :answer/id #uuid "25e59566-f703-5a9f-a0a6-83c58a53a3a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{2x}+2{e}^{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8099/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d1fa2e0-9c88-51a3-b933-c8c816cb081e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8099/selection/c3a41f59c04230b11372818321cc594550e1fc29de294c5d1c4649034da36d32" :answer-field/choices ["q-8099/selection/14dda16bf3677b40c9d18d46b6a541ed3bdbc1f25448258db1986eb44d9d45aa" "q-8099/selection/00460e20ed1d34c197a9be20e011dd597acdbfb2a07560e00454b71d68378cf5" "q-8099/selection/88feea0645bd98b57357f3aaa8e168684e33a9f5b1ef4970d8a733361ae568be" "q-8099/selection/c3a41f59c04230b11372818321cc594550e1fc29de294c5d1c4649034da36d32" "q-8099/selection/393fe52ac9ccbb50900a0186b5548c3ae356a1b24ddf8f51fb4d31101b3d16ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8099" :question/id #uuid "1cd59461-d6db-57c3-84e4-ef10e9a068c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-8099" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8y=6{e}^{4x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -8 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-2$ or $\\lambda =4$,  hence the complementary function ${y}_{c}$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{4x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $6{e}^{4x}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $4$, which coincides with one of the roots of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha x{e}^{4x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha (1+4x){e}^{4x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\alpha (8+16x){e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha (8+16x){e}^{4x}-2(\\alpha (1+4x){e}^{4x})-8\\alpha x{e}^{4x} & =6{e}^{4x} \\\\ (8+16x-2-8x-8x)\\alpha {e}^{4x} & =6{e}^{4x} \\\\ 6\\alpha {e}^{4x} & =6{e}^{4x} \\\\ 6\\alpha  & =6 \\\\ \\alpha  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{4x}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{4x}+x{e}^{4x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8099/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61611329-9ecd-5917-a11e-3b5effa69673"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8099"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8101/selection/08fe94f13ff386dc096c82e16f107ee0ec0072a4d2284dec1368a72acb2a8851" :answer/id #uuid "17b9366a-2d69-578d-8bd4-d6324254fc70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{3x}+B{e}^{4x}+\\frac{1}{3}x{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8101/selection/9634bcc42148a55dc542ed83f6f9074e87f2416c7e813d1647e0afff61f84d8e" :answer/id #uuid "9a8a472d-9a80-5857-b34c-b5808da6e09f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{-4x}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8101/selection/8aef97ba137cb5a44187b2f9637d6c4e9c012bedec495406d7497c3cfa1bfe99" :answer/id #uuid "dc219b6e-ce84-554b-865e-a99507d76bc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{-4x}+\\frac{1}{3}x{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8101/selection/7e951bdbf625f0f28d9ac5a91147ad6ce0979cd31b23727703ea61d3ff6dbad9" :answer/id #uuid "4ddf1218-be8d-53f5-84df-261301e41847" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{4x}+{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8101/selection/30f766ecfdde8e90fec381f272e93854470aefa160ce7fbafad8dc1bdb5bf35a" :answer/id #uuid "469c1f9f-1f1d-5a2a-8903-376cb5c18a26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{-4x}-{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8101/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "01776914-c596-531d-bed4-0103bd0cec77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8101/selection/9634bcc42148a55dc542ed83f6f9074e87f2416c7e813d1647e0afff61f84d8e" :answer-field/choices ["q-8101/selection/08fe94f13ff386dc096c82e16f107ee0ec0072a4d2284dec1368a72acb2a8851" "q-8101/selection/9634bcc42148a55dc542ed83f6f9074e87f2416c7e813d1647e0afff61f84d8e" "q-8101/selection/8aef97ba137cb5a44187b2f9637d6c4e9c012bedec495406d7497c3cfa1bfe99" "q-8101/selection/7e951bdbf625f0f28d9ac5a91147ad6ce0979cd31b23727703ea61d3ff6dbad9" "q-8101/selection/30f766ecfdde8e90fec381f272e93854470aefa160ce7fbafad8dc1bdb5bf35a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8101" :question/id #uuid "236244f2-a048-542e-8782-505037690d4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-8101" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+7\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+12y=21{e}^{3x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+7\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+12y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+7\\lambda +12 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)(\\lambda +4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-3$ or $\\lambda =-4$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{-4x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $21{e}^{3x}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $3$, which is not the root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {e}^{3x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=3\\alpha {e}^{3x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=9\\alpha {e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p}$, ${y}_{p}^{′}$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9\\alpha {e}^{3x}+7(3\\alpha {e}^{3x})+12(\\alpha {e}^{3x}) & =21{e}^{3x} \\\\ (9+21+12)\\alpha {e}^{3x} & =21{e}^{3x} \\\\ 42\\alpha  & =21 \\\\ \\alpha  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{-4x}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{3x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8101/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "03260b0d-f1c4-5c40-89dc-3de2d1017148"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8101"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8109/selection/570d202152afc866532e23546e1b08b4bf030683a4037a7951f713003002a2b0" :answer/id #uuid "39d846f5-99ea-5924-8d9b-bbaf8d873212" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+5{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8109/selection/1598870435cf6c464d9ef670dfce1103d2f29f7794a58ac94871d41d3ad94975" :answer/id #uuid "46dbb446-ed7a-52a3-b6ed-c4bb78c91ee3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-4{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+5{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8109/selection/882f62179d193bb3677600ec147c4639f757bc537787fe43b0e55c4804d44c02" :answer/id #uuid "0a213fe1-847e-59b5-bac0-ffa149a06c9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)-{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8109/selection/9c779ce1b42ac11767b28b6968c741a1a08d06d0c3c8befad623b9244aa90c35" :answer/id #uuid "77697a4b-3bb7-571a-a5b1-54977a6a468a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8109/selection/ec2c1bc146db46dd559f94341728767631e82eee8e3ad8799e67da75a7ef4466" :answer/id #uuid "7e243406-572c-569e-8035-55fd75af376f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{2x}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+5{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8109/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "795e3a97-b6a5-56be-8bf8-e6fbd7b383d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8109/selection/1598870435cf6c464d9ef670dfce1103d2f29f7794a58ac94871d41d3ad94975" :answer-field/choices ["q-8109/selection/570d202152afc866532e23546e1b08b4bf030683a4037a7951f713003002a2b0" "q-8109/selection/1598870435cf6c464d9ef670dfce1103d2f29f7794a58ac94871d41d3ad94975" "q-8109/selection/882f62179d193bb3677600ec147c4639f757bc537787fe43b0e55c4804d44c02" "q-8109/selection/9c779ce1b42ac11767b28b6968c741a1a08d06d0c3c8befad623b9244aa90c35" "q-8109/selection/ec2c1bc146db46dd559f94341728767631e82eee8e3ad8799e67da75a7ef4466"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8109" :question/id #uuid "43bc963a-bacb-5dc3-8983-c6b7ccb15e63" :question/math-academy-id "q-8109" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+8y=20{e}^{2x},\\,y(0)=1,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(0)=2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+8y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +8=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +8 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +4)-4+8 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2} & =-4 \\\\ \\lambda -2 & =\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =2\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c}(x) & ={e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $20{e}^{2x}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $2,$ which is not the root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {e}^{2x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=2\\alpha {e}^{2x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=4\\alpha {e}^{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\alpha {e}^{2x}-4(2\\alpha {e}^{2x})+8(\\alpha {e}^{2x}) & =20{e}^{2x} \\\\ \\alpha (4-8+8){e}^{2x} & =20{e}^{2x} \\\\ 4\\alpha {e}^{2x} & =20{e}^{2x} \\\\ 4\\alpha  & =20 \\\\ \\alpha  & =5\\text{ }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=5{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+5{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nNow let's find the constants $P$ and $Q.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=2.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2{e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+{e}^{2x}(-2P\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+2Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+10{e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=2$ into the above gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2P+2Q+10 & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $P=-4$ and $Q=0.$\n\nWe substitute this into the general particular integral and find that the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{2x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+0)+5{e}^{2x} \\\\  & =-4{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+5{e}^{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-8109/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "749a2a49-4181-5be7-b5ef-3e5f8d82219f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8109"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64236"] :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=10{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{x}+Bx{e}^{x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." :question/worked-solution "Since the complementary function is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{x}+Bx{e}^{x},$ we have that $\\lambda =1$ is the double root of the auxiliary equation.\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $10{e}^{x}.$  In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $1$, which coincides with the double root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {x}^{2}{e}^{x},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha ({x}^{2}+2x){e}^{x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\alpha ({x}^{2}+4x+2){e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha ({x}^{2}+4x+2){e}^{x}-2(\\alpha ({x}^{2}+2x){e}^{x})+(\\alpha {x}^{2}{e}^{x}) & =10{e}^{x} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+4x+2-2{x}^{2}-4x+{x}^{2})\\alpha {e}^{x} & =10{e}^{x} \\\\ 2\\alpha {e}^{x} & =10{e}^{x} \\\\ 2\\alpha  & =10 \\\\ \\alpha  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=5{x}^{2}{e}^{x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-93677/selection/16f261698690f79eb3171ed496ab5022403d67728def90a0b8ea3c773532ca6d" :answer/id #uuid "fb269b49-6a23-50e0-90ef-dd04a2945583" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-3{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93677/selection/4f110a84fb58764fba11eec1adb3b33dff55dc43736deb3d535dfd064b606bd3" :answer/id #uuid "2d6608f5-ff52-5a0c-a6a3-0e7887147c7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-2x{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93677/selection/9c9ae1a9a016f081542b3d4c2be0973ed123310f309ca470c46015598a9b9a51" :answer/id #uuid "c3da8036-662a-5e2e-88c4-f3e1af82cea2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=2{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93677/selection/44ab35e51798dd2ae821edc8db927343ccbd19411ea6b8f3a81af7e62025a6de" :answer/id #uuid "57bd919f-92a7-5801-89a1-76874e21333d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-3x{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93677/selection/0615e6fb2678a382416fdd30a05a436ab476ad3ec442df7c6f058b366607c4e3" :answer/id #uuid "d1bd506a-ea3b-599e-9a1e-9dd3460aba81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=4x{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93677/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bfa94eec-f01a-5bc3-93b4-d3937b5d4691" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93677/selection/0615e6fb2678a382416fdd30a05a436ab476ad3ec442df7c6f058b366607c4e3" :answer-field/choices ["q-93677/selection/16f261698690f79eb3171ed496ab5022403d67728def90a0b8ea3c773532ca6d" "q-93677/selection/4f110a84fb58764fba11eec1adb3b33dff55dc43736deb3d535dfd064b606bd3" "q-93677/selection/9c9ae1a9a016f081542b3d4c2be0973ed123310f309ca470c46015598a9b9a51" "q-93677/selection/44ab35e51798dd2ae821edc8db927343ccbd19411ea6b8f3a81af7e62025a6de" "q-93677/selection/0615e6fb2678a382416fdd30a05a436ab476ad3ec442df7c6f058b366607c4e3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93677" :question/id #uuid "94805db8-44e1-55e0-9567-e2835fac8614" :question/math-academy-id "q-93677" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=4{e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{2x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." :question/worked-solution "Since the complementary function is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{2x},$ the roots of the auxiliary equation are $\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =2.$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $4{e}^{2x}.$ In this case, the constant factor in the exponent is $2$, which coincides with one of the roots of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha x{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha (1+2x){e}^{2x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\alpha (4x+4){e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute ${y}_{p},$ ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and ${y}_{p}^{″}$ into the ODE and solve for $\\alpha :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha (4x+4){e}^{2x}-3(\\alpha (1+2x){e}^{2x})+2(\\alpha x{e}^{2x}) & =4{e}^{2x} \\\\ (4x+4-3-6x+2x)\\alpha {e}^{2x} & =4{e}^{2x} \\\\ \\alpha {e}^{2x} & =4{e}^{2x} \\\\ \\alpha  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=4x{e}^{2x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93677/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61611329-9ecd-5917-a11e-3b5effa69673"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93677"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
